&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BDR Manager&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Company Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Archera empowers organizations of all sizes to optimize their cloud costs through unique, short-term, insured commitments. Thousands of customers rely on Archera’s innovative FinTech solutions to increase their cloud ROI while accelerating revenue objectives and service agility.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Archera’s unique cloud rate insurance products and free FinOps platform enable teams to accurately predict and plan infrastructure growth, maximize commitment-based savings, and hedge against market demands and evolving cloud service provider offerings. Archera works closely with AWS, Microsoft Azure, and Google Cloud, along with a broad partner ecosystem, to help customers execute financially prudent cloud strategies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Archera is hiring a BDR Manager to lead and help scale the team that builds our sales pipeline. Reporting to the Director of Sales, you will manage a team of four BDRs of mixed seniority and own the qualified meetings (SQLs) they generate. This is a true player-coach role: you will spend real hours on the phones modeling what great outbound looks like, while coaching reps in the flow of the work, sharpening playbooks and sequences, and owning a weekly forecast with sales leadership. You will partner closely with Sales, Marketing, and RevOps to keep messaging sharp, target account lists fresh and researched, and the top of the funnel healthy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and coach a team of four BDRs of mixed seniority, running weekly one-on-ones that blend number review with real development, plus live call reviews and discovery listening; uplifting senior reps while patiently ramping more junior ones.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the team’s SQL output (qualified meetings set), starting each day with a pipeline pulse on meetings booked, calendar health, show-rates, and tracking every rep against their target.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay hands-on on the phones, modeling excellent outbound, jumping onto tricky prospects with more junior reps, and workshopping messaging with senior reps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and continuously refine the outbound engine: sequences, call and email playbooks, and researched, up-to-date target account lists with a clear thesis.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own weekly forecasting and pipeline reporting, partnering with the Director of Sales to walk through expected SQLs and diagnose what is driving any gaps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive improvements to messaging, sequencing, and personalization, using A/B testing and leading-indicator metrics to decide what lands best with respective prospects.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help hire, onboard, and ramp reps, deepening the team’s command of Archera’s domain, competitive and FinOps landscape, and buyer persona(s).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years carrying and hitting a quota as a BDR/SDR&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of successfully managing a BDR/SDR team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated leadership, coaching, and mentoring range. The ability to develop reps across the seniority spectrum.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Metrics-fluent: comfortable living in the data, forecasting off leading indicators rather than gut feel, and holding yourself and the team accountable to top-of-funnel metrics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record building and refining playbooks, sequences, and target account lists. Strategically improving process, not just running an existing one.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on fluency with a modern sales tech stack (e.g., Apollo, Nooks, Gong, Salesforce).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong command of outbound messaging and sequencing, with an eye for what makes outreach land.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience selling into technical or cloud/infrastructure buyers, and familiarity with FinOps, DevOps, and/or cloud infrastructure, is a major plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive salary and equity package&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401(k) plan&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible PTO and company holidays&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Remote-first culture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opportunity to shape and scale a category-defining FinTech platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Company Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Archera empowers organizations of all sizes to optimize their cloud costs through unique, short-term, insured Commitments. Hundreds of customers rely on Archera’s innovative FinTech solutions to increase their cloud ROI while accelerating revenue objectives and service agility.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Archera’s unique cloud rate products enable teams to maximize savings, hedge against usage changes and evolving cloud service provider offerings, and reinvest capital into top-line revenue initiatives. Archera works closely with AWS, Microsoft Azure, and Google Cloud, and a broad network of software and services partners to help each customer execute upon a bespoke, financially-prudent cloud growth and success strategy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Archera is looking for a Commercial Account Executive to own the full sales cycle across our commercial and mid-market segment. You’ll prospect into new accounts, run discovery and product demos, quantify savings opportunities, and close deals with both technical and financial stakeholders. This is a high-velocity, quota-carrying role for a curious, coachable seller who wants to grow while helping customers unlock meaningful cloud savings. You’ll partner closely with SDRs, Solutions Engineers, and leadership to build pipeline and move deals to close.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the end-to-end sales cycle for commercial and mid-market accounts, from prospecting through close&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prospect into target accounts and build pipeline through personalized, multi-channel outreach&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run discovery and demo calls, delivering tailored savings analyses that map Archera’s value to each prospect’s cloud environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Progress active deals, navigating technical and financial stakeholders across engineering, FinOps, and finance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build account plans and conduct account mapping to identify and engage key decision makers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with SDRs, Solutions Engineers, and marketing on account strategy and messaging&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain accurate pipeline, forecast, and activity data in Salesforce and the broader sales stack&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare presentations and represent Archera at events and conferences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuously incorporate coaching and market feedback to refine your approach&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of tech sales experience with a track record of successfully closing deals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of the tech sales motion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coachability — adaptable to change and able to incorporate new learnings promptly and effectively&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curiosity — digs deeper than surface-level learnings, objections, and pain points&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with a modern sales stack, including Salesforce, Gong, Apollo, Dripify, and Zoom&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI-enabled and proficient in applying AI tools to sell more effectively&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated executive presence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience selling to a highly technical persona&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience selling to cloud infrastructure and/or FinOps customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience at a FinOps, cloud infrastructure, observability, or cloud optimization company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cloud and/or FinOps certifications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;On-target earnings (OTE): $150,000–$200,000, with uncapped commission. This is a fully remote role based in the United States (East Coast preferred).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive salary and equity package&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401(k) plan&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible PTO policy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Remote-first culture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Annual wellness benefit&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opportunity to shape and scale a category-defining FinTech platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

