&lt;h3&gt;Company Overview&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Archera empowers organizations of all sizes to optimize their cloud costs through unique, short-term, insured commitments. Hundreds of customers rely on Archera&#39;s innovative FinTech solutions to increase their cloud ROI while accelerating revenue objectives and service agility.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Archera&#39;s unique cloud rate insurance products and free FinOps platform enable teams to accurately predict and plan infrastructure growth, maximize commitment-based savings, and hedge against market demands and evolving cloud service provider offerings. Archera works closely with AWS, Microsoft Azure, and Google Cloud, along with a broad partner ecosystem, to help customers execute financially prudent cloud strategies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Position Overview&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Forward Deployed Engineer, you sit where Archera&#39;s platform meets the field. This is an engineering role: you will write code, build integrations against partner and hyperscaler APIs, and own what you ship. You will also be the most technical person in the room with a distributor&#39;s engineering team, an AWS or Microsoft field counterpart, or a customer&#39;s Director of Cloud — explaining what Archera does at a deeper technical level, how other customers have successfully used Archera, and why the numbers hold. Both halves are the job.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will report to the Senior Director of Field Engineering &amp;amp; GTM Enablement and work across the full deal cycle: technical discovery and commitment modeling on an enterprise pursuit one week, integration delivery or a production escalation the next. You will partner closely with Technical Account Management, Partner Development, Alliances, Marketing, Product, and Engineering. Commitment purchases and exchanges stay with Platform Operations — you set and validate the strategy. Long-term hardening and the roadmap stay with Product and Engineering — you incubate, they productize. This role is remote within the United States, with light travel.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the technical owner on your engagements, from scoping a loosely defined problem through to something running in production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build integrations and prototypes against partner and hyperscaler APIs — time-boxed MVPs, microapps, and proofs of concept that prove an idea in front of a partner or customer, then hand validated work to Product and Engineering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Model and defend commitment strategy against live cloud usage — reservations, savings plans, Guaranteed Commitment (GRI) economics, exchange strategy, and fleet modernization — grounded in platform data you verified yourself and presented to Director- and VP-level stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take on the hardest technical problems that reach the field: complex onboarding, permissions and RBAC, billing-data integrity, and production escalations. That includes debugging live integrations directly with partner and hyperscaler engineering teams and driving fixes to closure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the technical overlay on large enterprise and partner pursuits, owning the technical conversation alongside Sales, Partner Development, and Alliances — including hyperscaler co-sell motions such as Azure IP Co-Sell and MACC positioning. You will influence revenue without carrying a quota.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Close the loop with Product and Engineering: reproduce issues, isolate root cause, file and manage tickets, and distill market feedback into evidence-backed patterns and prioritized feature requests.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own technical documentation — analyze it for gaps, verify it against actual platform behavior, and give GTM Enablement and Marketing the source material for partner and seller training and certification.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years in hands-on technical roles that include significant customer- or partner-facing work. Backgrounds that fit: forward deployed or field engineer, solutions architect, consulting engineer, technical founder, or an engineering lead at an MSP or cloud consultancy. Depth matters more than the count.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep hands-on Azure experience, including its commitment and discount constructs (reservations, savings plans, exchange mechanics) and the billing mechanics underneath them: cost exports, FOCUS schema, effective cost, and custom price sheets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working fluency with modern developer tooling — APIs, Git, scripting, IaC, and CI/CD — including daily use of AI coding assistants such as Claude Code. Come ready to walk through architecture you personally built and what broke.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to debug integration failures alongside a third party&#39;s engineering team and drive the fix to closure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The discipline to pressure-test your own numbers against source data before they reach a customer. A wrong savings figure in front of a CFO costs more than a slow one.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to move between audiences without losing accuracy — a technical design discussion in the morning, the same work explained to a CFO in the afternoon — plus comfort with incomplete information and the judgment to decide what is worth building and what is worth escalating.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Azure Solutions Architect Expert certification (AZ-305) or equivalent architecture depth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Nice-to-Haves&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Early-stage or scaling-startup experience where the role was defined by what needed doing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a channel or distribution motion — distributor, reseller, or CSP/MSP mechanics — and with hyperscaler marketplace and co-sell programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;FinOps Foundation certification (FinOps Practitioner or FOCUS Analyst) or equivalent cloud-cost discipline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Multi-cloud depth beyond Azure, across AWS or GCP commitment constructs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Published technical content: blog posts, talks, demos, or other technical evangelism.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Benefits&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive salary and equity package&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401(k) plan&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible PTO and company holidays&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Remote-first culture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opportunity to shape and scale a category-defining FinTech platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h1&gt;GM, AI Compute&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Company Overview&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Archera empowers organizations of all sizes to optimize their cloud costs through unique, short-term, insured commitments. Hundreds of customers rely on Archera&#39;s innovative FinTech solutions to increase their cloud ROI while accelerating revenue objectives and service agility.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Archera&#39;s unique cloud rate insurance products and free FinOps platform enable teams to accurately predict and plan infrastructure growth, maximize commitment-based savings, and hedge against market demands and evolving cloud service provider offerings. Archera works closely with AWS, Microsoft Azure, and Google Cloud, along with a broad partner ecosystem, to help customers execute financially prudent cloud strategies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Position Overview&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Archera is seeking a GM to run the customer side of a new compute product that gives developers and teams access to GPU and CPU capacity at better prices and on more flexible terms. You will run it like a startup inside Archera, owning positioning, developer adoption, go-to-market, and messaging. You will report to our product leader and work closely with our CEO and engineering. This is a full-time role. We strongly prefer candidates in the San Francisco Bay Area.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the positioning, roadmap, and outcomes for the customer side of a new compute product.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own developer adoption, from discovery and self-serve signup to paying usage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Test and run go-to-market playbooks to bring in demand.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Decide what the product sells next and to whom.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own messaging, marketing, and the product website.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with engineering on requirements, launches, and success metrics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of experience in product, growth, or go-to-market roles on technical products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has taken a developer-facing platform end to end, from build through launch and growth, with real go-to-market ownership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has done this as a GM, founder, or early product lead.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort writing positioning and customer-facing content yourself.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear written and verbal communication with technical and business audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Nice-to-Haves&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of GPUs, AI compute, and token-based pricing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience at an AI compute, GPU cloud, or inference provider.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with usage-based pricing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Benefits&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive salary and equity package&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401(k) plan&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible PTO and company holidays&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3 months of paid parental leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Remote-first culture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opportunity to shape and scale a category-defining FinTech platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Company Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Archera empowers organizations of all sizes to optimize their cloud costs through unique, short-term, insured commitments. Hundreds of customers rely on Archera&#39;s innovative FinTech solutions to increase their cloud ROI while accelerating revenue objectives and service agility.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Archera&#39;s unique cloud rate insurance products and free FinOps platform enable teams to accurately predict and plan infrastructure growth, maximize commitment-based savings, and hedge against market demands and evolving cloud service provider offerings. Archera works closely with AWS, Microsoft Azure, and Google Cloud, along with a broad partner ecosystem, to help customers execute financially prudent cloud strategies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Partner Development Manager, you will build and grow a book of channel partners who bring Archera to their customers. Reporting to the Director of Partner Development, you will recruit new partners — distributors, resellers, MSPs, systems integrators, and cloud consultancies — turn them into active, selling partners, and work alongside AWS, Microsoft, and Google Cloud field teams to generate partner-sourced pipeline and revenue.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a build role. You will not inherit an existing book; you will source your own partners and your own pipeline, with a Business Development Manager supporting partner recruiting and close partnership from Archera&#39;s Sales, Field Engineering, Marketing, and Partner Operations teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recruit, onboard, and activate new channel partners, and build the relationships that turn a signed agreement into a partner actively selling Archera.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generate partner-sourced and partner-influenced pipeline, and carry opportunities through to close alongside Archera&#39;s Sales team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and run joint go-to-market plans with partners and hyperscaler field teams, including co-sell motions and marketplace offers across AWS, Microsoft, and Google Cloud.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead partner enablement: train partner sales and FinOps teams on Archera&#39;s Guaranteed Commitments and FinOps platform, and deliver the presentations and demos that make partners confident selling Archera.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pitch Archera to partner and customer executives up to the C-suite, and speak credibly about Reserved Instances, Savings Plans, and commitment strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep pipeline, partner activity, and forecasts accurate in Salesforce, and report partner performance against pipeline and revenue goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Archera at partner, hyperscaler, and industry events, and work with Marketing on joint events, case studies, and co-marketing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years in partner development, channel sales, strategic alliances, or business development within cloud, SaaS, or cloud services. Backgrounds that fit: partner or channel manager at a distributor, a FinOps or cloud cost optimization provider, a cloud consultancy or MSP, or a hyperscaler partner organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of building a channel from the ground up — recruiting partners, enabling them, and turning them into measurable sourced pipeline and revenue.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep hands-on experience with at least one hyperscaler partner ecosystem (AWS, Microsoft Azure, or Google Cloud), including partner programs, co-sell motions, and marketplace.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of cloud economics and FinOps, including Reserved Instances, Savings Plans, and how commitments shape a customer&#39;s cloud bill.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confidence presenting to and pitching C-suite executives, and the range to move between a technical conversation and a business one.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to own a partner portfolio independently: setting priorities, running partner cadences, and keeping Salesforce current.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AWS, Azure, or Google Cloud certifications, or a FinOps Foundation certification.&lt;/li&gt;
